      <show id="873661688">
        <name>
          <![CDATA[Jerker]]>
        </name>
        <description>
          <![CDATA[<p><span><span><span><span><font size="4"><i><b>Strictly Limited Run from 26 Sept 2026</b></i></font></span></span></span></span></p><p><span><span><span><font size="3">Adam Roebuck presents</font></span></span></span></p><p><b><font size="5">Jerker</font></b></p><p><span><span><span><font size="3">by Robert Chelsey</font></span></span></span></p><p><font size="4">with&nbsp;<strong>PAUL DENNISON</strong> as <em>JR</em> &amp; <strong>JAMES LEE </strong>as <em>Bert</em></font><span><span><span><font size="3"></font></span></span></span></p><p><i><font size="3">​From the producer of <b>F**king Men, Afterglow (2019)</b>, and <b>Happy Ending</b> comes Robert Chesley&apos;s <b>JERKER</b>, a bold two-hander, making its highly anticipated Waterloo East Theatre premiere this Autumn,&nbsp;</font></i><span style="font-size:0.875rem;">40 year after its acclaimed premier in San Francisco.</span></p><p><span><span><span><b><i>JERKER</i></b></span></span> is a daring and seductive two-person drama about two strangers who connect through a series of late-night phone calls.&nbsp;</span><span>What begins as anonymous fantasy quickly sparks into something deeper. </span></p><p><span>Hidden from each other&rsquo;s sight, the men reveal secrets, fears, and longings through nothing but their voices.&nbsp;</span><span>Each call pulls them further into an intimate world where imagination becomes a lifeline, where the line between fantasy and genuine connection begins to blur, raising the question of who they really are to one another. </span></p><p><span>By turns playful, provocative, and unexpectedly tender, the play explores how intimacy can grow in isolation. It&rsquo;s a steamy, suspenseful journey into desire, vulnerability, and the power of being heard.</span></p><p><b>Cast:</b></p><p>JR - Paul Dennison&nbsp;</p><p>Bert - James Lee​​​​</p><p><b>Creatives:</b></p><p>Director: Henry Adams</p><p>Assistant Director/Intimacy Director: Alice Camarota</p><p>Set/Costume: Waterloo East Theatre</p><p>Lighting Design: Jonathan Simpson</p><p>Sound Design:&nbsp; Henry Adams &amp; Scott Michaels</p><p>QLab Programing: Dylan Salinger</p><p>Stage Manager: Jack Firman</p><p>Photography &amp; Videography: Scott Michaels&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><b><i><font color="#f61313">18+ Contains strong language.

Descriptive language of a sexual nature and nudity.</font></i></b></p><p><b><i><font color="#080808">Running Time approx. 90 minutes without an interval</font></i></b></p><p><span style="font-size:0.75rem;">JERKER is produced
by special arrangement with Broadway Play Publishing Inc, NYC www.broadwayplaypublishing.com</span></p>]]>
        </description>
